<title>FINLAND: FINNISH Q3 1996 NOMINAL WAGES UP 3.3 PCT YR/YR -SF.</title>
<headline>FINNISH Q3 1996 NOMINAL WAGES UP 3.3 PCT YR/YR -SF.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nominal wages rose 3.3 percent on average year-on-year in July-September 1996, Statistics Finland said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>The real earnings index rose 2.9 percent year-on-year, it said.  </p>
<p>&quot;The wage increases were mainly due to general pay rises in November last year,&quot; SF said.</p>
<p>Wages rose 3.2 percent in the private sector and 3.3 percent in the public sector, it said.</p>
<p>The average monthly salary was almost 10,600 markka, SF said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0248</p>
</text>
